{"id":"cor","name":"Cor","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:cor"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Cor","text":"This Hebrew word, untranslated, denotes a round vessel used as a measure both for liquids and solids. It was equal to one homer, and contained ten ephahs in dry and ten baths in liquid measure (Ezek. 45:14). The Rabbins estimated the cor at forty-five gallons, while Josephus estimated it at about eighty-seven. In 1 Kings 4:22; 5:11; 2 Chr. 2:10; 27:5, the original word is rendered “measure.”"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3734","lemma":"כֹּר","xlit":"kôr","gloss":"a deep round vessel","kjv":"cor, measure. Aramaic the same","count":6,"share":0.86},{"strong":"H2406","lemma":"חִטָּה","xlit":"chiṭṭâh","gloss":"wheat, whether the grain or the plant","kjv":"wheat","count":3,"share":0.43},{"strong":"H1324","lemma":"בַּת","xlit":"bath","gloss":"a bath or Hebrew measure of liquids","kjv":"bath","count":2,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H8081","lemma":"שֶׁמֶן","xlit":"shemen","gloss":"grease, especially liquid","kjv":"anointing, fat, fruitful, oil","count":3,"share":0.43},{"strong":"H8184","lemma":"שְׂעֹרָה","xlit":"sᵉʻôrâh","gloss":"barley","kjv":"barley","count":2,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H505","lemma":"אֶלֶף","xlit":"ʼeleph","gloss":"hence a thousand","kjv":"thousand","count":3,"share":0.43}],"verses":["1Kgs.4.22","1Kgs.5.11","2Chr.2.10","2Chr.27.5","Ezra.7.22","Ezek.45.14","Luke.16.7"],"related":[{"id":"measure","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.051,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"barley","type":"lexical","strong":"H2406","why":"both lead with חִטָּה (H2406)"},{"id":"rye-spelt-r-v","type":"lexical","strong":"H2406","why":"both lead with חִטָּה (H2406)"},{"id":"wheat","type":"lexical","strong":"H2406","why":"both lead with חִטָּה (H2406)"}],"works":[]}
